==================================================================
DAY 22 - PART A: THEORY
ConfigMaps: Separating Configuration from Images
Time: 30-40 minutes
==================================================================

1. WHY SEPARATE CONFIG?
-----------------------
The same image should run in dev, test and prod. What changes between
them is CONFIGURATION: database host, log level, feature flags, config
files. If config is baked into the image you need a different image
per environment. Bad.

Rule (from the "12-factor app"): build once, configure per
environment at runtime.


2. WHAT IS A CONFIGMAP?
-----------------------
A namespaced object holding NON-SECRET key/value data:

  apiVersion: v1
  kind: ConfigMap
  metadata:
    name: app-config
  data:
    LOG_LEVEL: "debug"
    DB_HOST: "postgres.db.svc.cluster.local"
    app.properties: |
      color=blue
      max_items=50

Max size: 1 MiB. Values are always strings (quote numbers/booleans).


3. FOUR WAYS TO CREATE ONE
--------------------------
  k create cm app-config --from-literal=LOG_LEVEL=debug
  k create cm app-config --from-file=app.properties
  k create cm app-config --from-env-file=app.env
  YAML + k apply   (preferred: stored in Git)


4. THREE WAYS TO USE ONE IN A POD
---------------------------------
a) Single env var:
     env:
     - name: LOG_LEVEL
       valueFrom:
         configMapKeyRef:
           name: app-config
           key: LOG_LEVEL

b) All keys as env vars:
     envFrom:
     - configMapRef:
         name: app-config

c) Mounted as files (each key becomes a file):
     volumes:
     - name: cfg
       configMap:
         name: app-config
     containers:
     - volumeMounts:
       - name: cfg
         mountPath: /etc/app        -> /etc/app/LOG_LEVEL, /etc/app/app.properties

   Mount only one key at a specific path with "subPath" (but subPath
   mounts do NOT get updates).


5. WHAT HAPPENS WHEN A CONFIGMAP CHANGES?
-----------------------------------------
  Env vars        NOT updated. Read once at container start.
                  -> need a restart (k rollout restart deploy/x)
  Mounted files   Updated automatically after ~1 minute (kubelet sync).
                  The app must re-read the file to notice.
  subPath mounts  NOT updated.

Common pattern: put a hash of the config in a pod annotation so any
config change triggers a rollout (Helm does this, Week 8).


6. IMMUTABLE CONFIGMAPS
-----------------------
  immutable: true
Can't be changed (only deleted/recreated). Protects against accidents
and reduces API load in big clusters. Use versioned names:
app-config-v2.


7. ENVIRONMENT FROM THE POD ITSELF (DOWNWARD API)
-------------------------------------------------
You used this on Day 16 (POD_NAME). Other fields:
  metadata.namespace, status.podIP, spec.nodeName,
  requests/limits via resourceFieldRef.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- Build once, configure at runtime.
- env / envFrom / volume mount.
- Env vars need a restart; mounted files update (~1 min).
